### What the page covers

| Section | Content |
|--------|---------|
| **Purpose** | AI judgment on whether Python-emitted HTML looks intentional vs nesting soup; PDCA tied to `render_section`, `ks_hash_attrs`, contracts |
| **Passing signals** | `render_section` shells, heading ladder, hash attrs, KS spacing tokens, shared helpers, optional-region omission |
| **Failing signals** | Wrapper soup, `h1`→`h4` jumps, ghost sections, ad-hoc chrome, hash afterthought |
| **Before example** | Failing: nested unclassed `<div>`s, inline margins, `h1` then card `h4`, no `forge-card` / `<section>` |
| **After example** | Passing: `forge-divider`, `<section class="mb-5">`, `section-label`, `h2`, `forge-card breathe-static`, `card-label`, `h3`, `forge-support` |
| **Evidence & remediation** | Capture paths, DOM, contracts; 7-step remediate ending in `DET.*` proposals |
| **Related rules** | `DET.PY.KS_HASH_ATTRS`, `DET.PY.OPTIONAL_REGIONS`, `DET.SECTION.HEADING`, `DET.SECTION.SINGLE_JOB`, `DET.HASH.MARKERS`, `AI.CONTRACT.IMPLEMENTATION_USEFULNESS` |

